cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "7G Multi-Medium Backhaul and Self-Scaling CDN Simulator"
abstract: >-
  An early-stage, single-author research prototype that simulates
  application-session continuity across heterogeneous microwave, HF, satellite,
  mobile, Wi-Fi, and drone-relay links, together with adaptive MTU,
  protocol-inspired mobility, carrier bonding, self-scaling CDN, edge
  orchestration, and a quantum-key-resource abstraction. One transport scenario
  (two-path handover with a constant-bit-rate UDP stream) has been
  cross-validated against an independent ns-3.49 implementation: the queue-free
  model agrees within 0.02 percent while links are lightly loaded, and its
  6.5-point delivery overstatement under handover overload is corrected by a
  bounded FIFO queue model (see docs/external-validation.md). Wireless PHY/MAC
  behaviour, TCP/MPTCP transport, trace calibration, and the CDN/cloud
  submodels remain unvalidated. A controlled ablation finds no goodput
  advantage from predictive pressure forecasting. As of version 0.1.0 there
  has been no external issue, pull request, fork contribution, or citation, and
  the work has not been peer reviewed. The prototype is intended for hypothesis
  generation, replication attempts, and methodological critique, not as evidence
  of deployed-network performance.
authors:
  - family-names: Nikolic
    given-names: Milan
version: 0.1.0
